## 2. Automation Scripts

### A. Repository Metadata & Channel Synchronization

Create `/usr/local/bin/sync-ptf-repo.sh` to update repository indexes and initiate MLM channel ingestion:

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

REPO_DIR="/var/lib/containers/storage/volumes/srv-www/_data/htdocs/pub/ptf_repo/mls7"
CHANNEL_LABEL="custom-ptf-mls7_ltss-x86_64"
LOG_FILE="/var/log/ptf-sync-automation.log"

exec >> "${LOG_FILE}" 2>&1

echo "=== Starting PTF sync at $(date) ==="

if [ -d "${REPO_DIR}" ]; then
  createrepo_c --update "${REPO_DIR}"
else
  echo "ERROR: Directory ${REPO_DIR} not found!" >&2
  exit 1
fi

echo "Triggering spacewalk-repo-sync for channel: ${CHANNEL_LABEL}..."
if command -v mgrctl >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  mgrctl exec -- spacewalk-repo-sync --channel "${CHANNEL_LABEL}" --type yum
else
  spacewalk-repo-sync --channel "${CHANNEL_LABEL}" --type yum
fi

echo "=== Sync completed successfully at $(date) ==="

```

Set script permissions:

```bash
chmod 750 /usr/local/bin/sync-ptf-repo.sh

```

