## 4. Fleet Deployment Options

### Option A: Direct System Group Assignment (Standard Fleet)

1. Navigate to **Systems > System Groups > MLS7-Fleet > Software > Channels** in the MLM Web UI and subscribe the group to `custom-ptf-mls7_ltss-x86_64`.
2. Dispatch package rollout across all target minions via Salt:

```bash
# Via Salt pkg module:
mgrctl exec -- salt -G 'systemgroup:MLS7-Fleet' pkg.install <ptf-package-name>

# Alternatively, run clean cached installation directly:
mgrctl exec -- salt -G 'systemgroup:MLS7-Fleet' cmd.run "yum clean expire-cache && yum install -y <ptf-package-name>"

```

---

### Option B: Zero-Rebuild Injection into Frozen CLM Environments

Avoids triggering full CLM rebuild cycles by injecting hotfixes directly into active, frozen lifecycle clones.

1. Locate the active target environment channel label:
```bash
spacecmd -u admin -p <PWD> -- softwarechannel_list | grep "clm-.*-custom-ptf"

```


2. Inject the verified PTF RPM directly into the target CLM channel:
```bash
spacecmd -u admin -p <PWD> -- softwarechannel_addpackages <CLM_TARGET_CHANNEL> "<ptf-package-name>*"

```


3. Trigger client updates immediately across the target fleet:
```bash
mgrctl exec -- salt -G 'systemgroup:MLS7-Fleet' cmd.run "yum clean expire-cache && yum install -y <ptf-package-name>"

```



